# Version pins for the toolchain (feat-5-foundation-monorepo-ci, REQ-003).
#
# This is the one source of truth for the versions of the tools. The install
# scripts (.specmgr/feat/feat-5-foundation-monorepo-ci/bin/) read it. The CI
# workflow repeats the versions as inputs of the setup actions, and a `just`
# recipe checks that both are the same (ACC-013).
#
# Format: KEY=value, no spaces, no quotes. A shell can source this file.
#
# Checksums: the values are copied from the files that the vendors publish
# (Temurin: the API of Adoptium; Maven: the .sha512 file; Node: SHASUMS256.txt;
# pnpm: the digest of the GitHub release; just: SHA256SUMS; npm and Maven Central:
# the checksum of the release). The Python tools have no checksum in this file: their
# lock files in tools/python/ have them. A change of a version must change the
# checksum, or the lock file, in the same commit. CODEOWNERS covers this file.
#
# What is checked with a checksum, and what is not (finding G2 of the review):
#
#   Install scripts (machine of the author): the JDK, Maven, Node, pnpm and just
#   are compared with the checksum of the download (JDK_SHA256, MAVEN_SHA512,
#   NODE_SHA256, PNPM_SHA256, JUST_SHA256).
#
#   The tools that the gates start in CI and on the machine of the author are
#   checked at run time:
#     - The Python tools (specmgr, PyYAML, license-expression with boolean.py;
#       feat-22-python-tools-lockfile): CHECKED, with all their dependencies. The lock
#       files in tools/python/ have the exact version and the sha256 of each file of each
#       package (44 packages for specmgr, 1 for PyYAML, 2 for license-expression). The gate
#       scripts install them with `uv pip install --require-hashes --only-binary :all:` in
#       a virtual environment of PYTHON_VERSION, so uv stops for a wrong hash, for a package
#       with no hash and for a package that is not in the file. No source archive is built.
#       This file has the version of each tool only (SPECMGR_VERSION, PYYAML_VERSION,
#       LICENSE_EXPRESSION_VERSION) and no checksum of them. `just check-pins` compares the
#       lock files with these versions (the procedure to change a version is in
#       tools/python/README.md).
#     - @cyclonedx/cdxgen (feat-16-cdxgen-lockfile): CHECKED, with all its
#       dependencies. tools/sbom/ is a pnpm project with one dependency and a
#       lock file that has an integrity value for each package (199 packages for
#       12.9.0, and 187 are installed on linux-x64). sbom.sh installs it with `pnpm install
#       --frozen-lockfile --ignore-scripts`, and pnpm compares each tarball with
#       the lock file. `just check-pins` compares package.json and the lock file
#       with CDXGEN_VERSION and CDXGEN_INTEGRITY of this file, so a change of only
#       one of the three places stops the check (the procedure to change the
#       version is in tools/sbom/README.md). Limit: a wrong integrity value of an
#       OPTIONAL dependency does not stop the install. pnpm does not install that
#       package, and the package does not run.
#     - @stoplight/spectral-cli (feat-6-contracts-openapi-pipeline, the OpenAPI linter): CHECKED, with all its
#       dependencies, as cdxgen. tools/spectral/ is a pnpm project with one dependency and a lock file that has
#       an integrity value for each package (242 packages). The gate script tools/gates/lint.sh installs it with
#       `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile --ignore-scripts`. `just check-pins` compares package.json and the lock
#       file with SPECTRAL_VERSION and SPECTRAL_INTEGRITY of this file (the procedure to change the version is
#       in tools/spectral/README.md). Spectral does not go to users (rule A), so its tree is not in the SBOM.
#     - oasdiff (feat-6-contracts-openapi-pipeline, Task 115.100, the tool for breaking changes of the OpenAPI
#       file): CHECKED, the download only. oasdiff is a Go binary with no dependency and no package manager.
#       tools/gates/breaking-changes.sh downloads the release file oasdiff_<OASDIFF_VERSION>_linux_amd64.tar.gz
#       from GitHub, compares its sha256 with OASDIFF_SHA256 before it unpacks the file, and puts the binary in
#       build/tools/ (the folder is not in git). The gates run on Linux x86_64 only (a runner of GitHub, and the
#       machine of the author, as the install scripts for just and Node), so there is one checksum, and the
#       script stops on another platform. `just check-pins` compares OASDIFF_VERSION and OASDIFF_SHA256 with the
#       file tools/breaking/oasdiff-checksums.txt, which is the file `checksums.txt` of the release (the
#       procedure to change the version is in tools/breaking/README.md), so a change of only one place stops the
#       check.
#     - cyclonedx-maven-plugin: sbom.sh compares the sha256 of the jar in the local
#       repository with CYCLONEDX_MAVEN_PLUGIN_SHA256 before the plugin makes the
#       SBOM. `just check-pins` compares CYCLONEDX_MAVEN_PLUGIN_SHA256 with the
#       second place, tools/sbom/cyclonedx-maven-plugin.sha256 (ACC-011). The dependencies of the
#       plugin are not checked (GitHub issue #23).
#     - openapi-generator-maven-plugin (feat-6-contracts-openapi-pipeline, Task 120.105): the same way. The
#       gates `just generate`, `just compile` and `just api-docs` compare the sha256 of the jar in the local
#       repository with OPENAPI_GENERATOR_MAVEN_PLUGIN_SHA256 and with the second place,
#       tools/generate/openapi-generator-maven-plugin.sha256, before they start the plugin, and `just check-pins`
#       compares OPENAPI_GENERATOR_MAVEN_PLUGIN_VERSION with the version in backend/pom.xml, and
#       OPENAPI_GENERATOR_MAVEN_PLUGIN_SHA256 with the second place (ACC-011). The dependencies of the
#       plugin are not checked (GitHub issue #23, the issue stays open for a full pinning). What the plugin (and
#       Kubb) make IS checked, though: `just check-generated` (the CI job of the same name, feat-6 Task 130.100)
#       makes the generated code again and compares it with HEAD, so a changed dependency that changes the output
#       stops the pull request, and the owner then sees the change of the generated code in the diff.
#     - Kubb, Zod and TypeScript (feat-6-contracts-openapi-pipeline, Task 120.110): CHECKED, with all their
#       dependencies. frontend/ is a pnpm module with a lock file that has an integrity value for each package
#       (102 packages). The gates install it with `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile --ignore-scripts`. `just check-pins`
#       compares frontend/package.json and the lock file with the keys KUBB_*, ZOD_* and TYPESCRIPT_* of this file.
#       The generated Zod code is compared with HEAD by `just check-generated` (see above).
#     - The CI jobs of feat-6 (feat-6-contracts-openapi-pipeline, Task 130.110): `lint` (Node, pnpm), `breaking-changes`
#       (uv; the download of oasdiff), `check-generated`, `compile` (Java, Node, pnpm) and `api-docs` (Java) have the
#       versions of this file in the inputs of the setup actions (JDK_VERSION, NODE_VERSION, PNPM_VERSION, UV_VERSION,
#       JUST_VERSION), and `just check-pins` compares them. The job `test-gates` has the Java, Node and pnpm steps
#       too, because its tests start the real tools.
#     - uv itself, the Python build that uv downloads and the GitHub Actions: UV_VERSION
#       has no checksum (the action astral-sh/setup-uv downloads it), and the actions
#       are pinned to a commit SHA.
#
# JDK: Eclipse Temurin 21 (LTS), GPL-2.0-only WITH Classpath-exception-2.0
JDK_VERSION=21.0.13+9
JDK_SHA256=d7f5d5cf865a2902b70ff549b97586a7d3f234e016f041ab447ea740c7d66d1c

# Maven (the 3.x line; Maven 4 is a release candidate), Apache-2.0
