# The test tools of the Maven module (feat-7-verification-architecture-tools, Phase 110, Tasks 110.100 and
# 110.130). The licenses are in the license table of the plan (JUnit and jqwik are EPL-2.0, the class
# Review, with the deviation DEC 93a6d588-e002-4daf-9a47-45e2d77786e9; Testcontainers is MIT; the JDBC
# driver is BSD-2-Clause). Every test tool is in <scope>test</scope> in backend/pom.xml, so the cyclonedx
# plugin (includeTestScope, the default false) keeps them out of the SBOM. backend/pom.xml must have the
# same versions (just check-pins checks it, check_pins.py: check_maven_test_pins). JUnit is the 5.x line
# (and not the 6.x line, the one that the phase 100 looked at): jqwik 1.10.2 needs the JUnit Platform
# 1.14.x. Testcontainers is the 1.21.x line: the junit-jupiter module has no 2.x release.
JUNIT_VERSION=5.14.4
TESTCONTAINERS_VERSION=1.21.4
POSTGRESQL_VERSION=42.7.14
JQWIK_VERSION=1.10.2
MAVEN_SUREFIRE_PLUGIN_VERSION=3.6.1

# The mutation tool of the Maven module (feat-7-verification-architecture-tools, Phase 120, Task 120.100).
# PIT (org.pitest:pitest-maven, the build plugin) and the JUnit5 support of PIT
# (org.pitest:pitest-junit5-plugin, a dependency of the plugin: pitest-maven loads the test framework plugins
# from its own classpath, and not from the test classpath of the module). The license is in the license table of
# the plan (Apache-2.0, the class Permitted, as the core of PIT that the phase 100 checked). backend/pom.xml must
# have the same versions (just check-pins checks it, check_pins.py: check_maven_test_pins).
PIT_VERSION=1.30.2
PIT_JUNIT5_PLUGIN_VERSION=1.2.3

# The architecture tools of the Maven module (feat-7-verification-architecture-tools, Phase 130, Tasks
# 130.100 and 130.120). Every tool is in <scope>test</scope> in backend/pom.xml, so the cyclonedx
# plugin (includeTestScope, the default false) keeps it out of the SBOM. backend/pom.xml must have the
# same versions (just check-pins checks it, check_pins.py: check_maven_test_pins). The licenses are in
# the license table of the plan (Apache-2.0, the class Permitted, as the row Spring Modulith, the row
# ArchUnit and the row Structurizr tools that the phase 100 checked).
# Spring Modulith is the 1.4.x line and not the 2.x line (2.1.2, the last general-availability release):
# the core of the 2.x line has the dependencies spring-core and spring-context 7.0.9, and the module
# has the Spring Framework 6.2.19 line (the plan records the decision). The core of 1.4.14 has the
# dependencies spring-core and spring-context 6.2.19, the same versions as the module. The jar
# org.springframework.boot:spring-boot (SPRING_BOOT_VERSION) is a dependency of the code of Spring
# Modulith 1.4.14 that the POM of the artifact does not declare: the factory ApplicationModules.of(...)
# calls the class ConfigDataEnvironmentPostProcessor of this jar in each start (a start without the jar
# stops with NoClassDefFoundError). The version 3.5.16 is the one of the 3.5.x line that the 1.4.x line
# of Spring Modulith has (the optional dependency spring-boot-autoconfigure of the core is 3.5.16), and
# its dependencies are spring-core and spring-context 6.2.19, the versions of the module.
SPRING_MODULITH_VERSION=1.4.14
SPRING_BOOT_VERSION=3.5.16
# ArchUnit (the two artifacts com.tngtech.archunit:archunit and com.tngtech.archunit:archunit-junit5).
# The core of Spring Modulith has the dependency archunit 1.4.2, and the module names 1.5.1: the
# resolution of Maven gives 1.5.1 (the nearest dependency wins).
ARCHUNIT_VERSION=1.5.1
# The reader of the workspace of model/ (the artifact com.structurizr:structurizr-client, the JSON
# reader and the model classes of structurizr-core). The module has no product code and no other
# reader of the workspace, so the client artifact (and not the DSL artifact structurizr-dsl, that has
# the client as a dependency) is in the module. The phase 100 looked at the library com.structurizr:
# structurizr 6.2.4 (the POM aggregator of the 6.x line, that has no jar): the artifact with the
# reader is structurizr-client 6.2.4 (the plan records the identification).
STRUCTURIZR_VERSION=6.2.4

# The test tools of the pnpm module (feat-7-verification-architecture-tools, Phase 110, Tasks 110.110 to
# 110.130). Each value is the version and the integrity value of the npm package (the value of
# `dist.integrity` of the registry). frontend/package.json (exact versions, no range) and
# frontend/pnpm-lock.yaml must have the same values (just check-pins checks it, check_pins.py:
# check_frontend). Change all three places in one commit: frontend/README.md. The licenses are in the
# license table of the plan (Vitest and fast-check are MIT, Playwright is Apache-2.0, axe-core is
# MPL-2.0, the class Review, with the deviation DEC 93a6d588-e002-4daf-9a47-45e2d77786e9). cdxgen includes
# the devDependencies in the SBOM of the frontend, and MPL-2.0 is not in the permitted list: sbom.sh
# removes the pinned axe-core from the SBOM after cdxgen made it (rule A: the tool does not go to users;
# see tools/sbom/README.md, the section The exclusion of axe-core).
# vite is a direct devDependency of the module (and not only a peer that pnpm resolves): vitest and the
# tree of Kubb take vite as a dependency or a peer, and the resolution of pnpm of the peer without a pin
# brings the tree of vite 8 with the package lightningcss (MPL-2.0, not in the permitted list, and no DEC
# of the owner for it). The pin is the 7.x line (in the range of vitest and of Kubb), and a clean lock file
# (a new pnpm install, not a change of the old lock file) resolves the tree without lightningcss.
